# Trust for one host only: earthquake.phivolcs.dost.gov.ph (21 Oct 2026; read by ws_quake_phivolcs in widgets.php).
# PHIVOLCS's server sends its own certificate without the intermediate that signed it, so a strict client (PHP's
# OpenSSL, Linux curl) cannot build the chain. These are the two public certificates it is missing:
#   GlobalSign RSA OV SSL CA 2018  (from the address in PHIVOLCS's certificate, secure.globalsign.com; until Nov 2028)
#     SHA-256 B6:76:FF:A3:17:9E:88:12:09:3A:1B:5E:AF:EE:87:6A:E7:A6:AA:F2:31:07:8D:AD:1B:FB:21:CD:28:93:76:4A
#   GlobalSign Root CA - R3        (the root it chains to, as in the usual CA bundles; until Mar 2029)
#     SHA-256 CB:B5:22:D7:B7:F1:27:AD:6A:01:13:86:5B:DF:1C:D4:10:2E:7D:07:59:AF:63:5A:7C:F4:72:0D:C9:63:C5:3B
# Verification stays on. If PHIVOLCS changes certificate authority, reading it fails and the widget shows USGS alone.
